 "how_to_mine": [
  "Follow this plan exactly. Each lens agent reads only its pages (all are in the corpus; read them with `show <source_id> --around TEXT` or `--lines A:B`, tables with `tables <source_id>`), answers its demand items, and records each item as filled (fact ids), contradicted (what the page says instead) or not-found (where you looked).",
  "Write facts in files of 10 to 25 facts: _build/work/31-messaging/facts-<lens>-NN.json, then `facts add --file <that file> --by mine-31-<lens>`. Table rows and value lines: prefer `facts adopt` (--table/--row, --sentence, --heading). Every quote is copied verbatim from the page snapshot (.txt), never from full.md (full.md hits are pointers) and never from memory.",
  "Fact service keys: `sqs`, `sns`, `eventbridge` (EventBridge Scheduler and Pipes facts use `eventbridge`). Ids start with the service key, for example `sqs-visibility-timeout-max`. A fact about another service (S3 Event Notifications: `s3`; Lambda event source mapping: `lambda`; EC2 Auto Scaling SQS policy: `ec2-auto-scaling`; Amazon MQ: check `registry show 32`; Kinesis: check `registry show 34`) is added only after `facts list --service <key>` shows no verified fact that already answers it; reuse the existing id in the demand record when one exists.",
  "Every hard fact (number, limit, default, price, date, can/cannot, only/always/never) carries `question` (the demand question it answers) and at least two displays for kinds behavior, capability, restriction and default (brief gate B12). A display of a number-free fact is a verbatim phrase of at most 8 words from its quote (RULINGS 2026-10-11).",
  "Changes: a fact touched by a change item sets `changed` (date, old value only if a saved page states it verbatim) and `change_items`; a feature GA after 2026-07-15 gets the note `not examinable yet` (SNS 1 MiB opt-in 2026-09-18; EventBridge Custom Event Bus relaunch 2026-09-24). Current truth comes from the guide and quotas pages; What's New pages and history rows give dates and deltas only.",
  "Where two AWS pages disagree (see brief research_input.conflicts_seen_at_plan), add the fact from the page that is current truth and record the other page in the demand note; do not add both values as competing facts.",
  "Case-study facts have kind `case-study` and a quote of at most 25 words."
 ],
